    "narrative": "The Ghost Ride the WHIP lineup is anchored today by **Corbin Carroll**, who boasts the day's peak efficiency at 81.08. Facing a favorable matchup against Randy V\u00e1squez (4.80 xERA), **Corbin Carroll** benefits from a massive 19% boost due to the SP\u2019s skill deficiency, making him an auto-start despite a minor park penalty. We are also leaning heavily into our speed-first philosophy with **Brice Turang** (66.27). While his raw projection is solid, the 4% efficiency kicker derived from the pitcher\u2019s slow delivery makes **Brice Turang** a premier target to steal bags against a favorable RHP/LHP setup. **Isaac Paredes** (63.82) is another core play, leveraging a 10% park boost and a significant platoon advantage to solidify the hot corner, while **James Wood** (61.74) remains a lineup lock\u2014his elite xwOBA effectively cancels out the defensive risk posed by the opposing backstop, even against a tough arm like Sean Manaea.\n\nOur toughest decision involved keeping **Vinnie Pasquantino** (41.02) on the bench. He hovered near the marginal threshold, but the 15% penalty from the platoon disadvantage against lefty Brandon Messick ultimately pushed him below the floor set by our starters. We are monitoring the status of **Jose Caballero** (53.81); his score is currently dampened by a projected #9 spot in the lineup, and we are proceeding with caution until the official card is posted. Meanwhile, we remain wary of **Trevor Story** (44.29) as he faces the stiff challenge of Shota Imanaga; he barely cleared the bench cut and serves only as a placeholder given our limited depth today. \n\nAs we approach the final stretch of the season, our roster remains thinned by the absence of **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Mickey Moniak**, and **Seiya Suzuki**, who provide no relief for our active starters. We continue to manage our remaining game caps carefully, trusting that high-efficiency bats like **Griffin Conine** (60.91)\u2014who jumps into the lineup with a stellar 18% SP skill advantage\u2014will provide the necessary production to outpace the field. Our depth pieces like **Tyler Soderstrom**, **Max Muncy**, **Gabriel Moreno**, **Dalton Rushing**, and **Edwin Arroyo** are currently sidelined as we prioritize the elite sprint speed and matchup-driven metrics provided by our active starters.",
